#!/bin/sh /etc/rc.common
# NFT TTL64 Controller (IPv4+IPv6)
# Integrated for luci-app-nft-ttl by SopekSemprit
# Base: ttl64ipv4v6.nft + UCI control

START=99
USE_PROCD=1
PROG=/usr/sbin/nft
NFT_FILE="/tmp/ttl64ipv4v6.nft"

start_service() {
	enable=$(uci get nftttl.settings.enable 2>/dev/null)
	value=$(uci get nftttl.settings.ttl_value 2>/dev/null)
	[ -z "$value" ] && value=64

	if [ "$enable" = "1" ]; then
		logger -t nftttl "Starting TTL changer (IPv4+IPv6) with TTL=$value"

		# Write dynamic nft rules
		cat <<EOF > $NFT_FILE
table inet ttlcontrol {
	chain mangle_forward {
		type filter hook forward priority mangle; policy accept;
		oifname "wwan0_1" ip ttl set $value
		oifname "wwan0_1" ip6 hoplimit set $value
	}
}
EOF

		# Flush and load ruleset
		$PROG flush table inet ttlcontrol 2>/dev/null
		$PROG -f $NFT_FILE
	else
		logger -t nftttl "TTL changer disabled"
		$PROG flush table inet ttlcontrol 2>/dev/null
	fi
}

stop_service() {
	logger -t nftttl "Stopping TTL changer"
	$PROG flush table inet ttlcontrol 2>/dev/null
}

reload_service() {
	stop_service
	start_service
}
